00:47:38.810 --> 00:47:43.460
<v Ira Glass>If this seems like an extreme response to you, reporter Graham Rayman confirms, it is.
<v Ira Glass>如果你觉得这是一种极端的反应，记者格雷姆·雷曼（Graham Rayman）证实，确实如此。

00:47:43.460 --> 00:47:48.810
<v Graham Rayman>Yeah, it's very extreme for going home from work early-- an hour early.
<v Graham Rayman>是的，对于提前下班——提前一个小时——来说，这非常极端。

00:47:48.810 --> 00:48:08.660
<v Ira Glass>An officer asks Adrian if he wants medical aid-- an EMT to come check him out. Adrian's blood pressure turns out to be sky high. They offer to take him to a hospital, but not his local hospital-- to one that he's never heard of. And he doesn't get what they're up to, and he refuses medical attention. Under the law, they should leave him alone. But for some reason, they will not take no for an answer.
<v Ira Glass>一名警官问阿德里安是否需要医疗援助——让急救人员（EMT）来给他检查一下。结果发现阿德里安的血压高得离谱。他们提出带他去医院，但不是去他当地的医院——而是去一个他从未听说过的医院。他搞不懂他们在搞什么名堂，于是拒绝了医疗救助。根据法律，他们应该离他远点。但出于某种原因，他们就是不肯罢休。

