<v Michael Marino>--listen to me. Now you have a choice. You get up like a man and put your shoes on and walk into that bus--
<v Michael Marino>——听我说。现在你有一个选择。你像个男人一样站起来，穿上鞋子，走进那辆救护车——

00:48:43.810 --> 00:48:44.650
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>Like a man.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>像个男人一样。

00:48:44.650 --> 00:48:50.750
<v Michael Marino>--like a man. Or son, they're going to treat you as an EDP and that means handcuffs. And I do not want to see that happen to a cop.
<v Michael Marino>——像个男人一样。否则，年轻人，他们会把你当作情绪困扰人员（EDP）对待，这意味着要戴上手铐。我不想看到这种事发生在一个警察身上。

00:48:50.750 --> 00:48:51.880
<v Ira Glass>EDP is?
<v Ira Glass>EDP是什么？

00:48:51.880 --> 00:48:53.620
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>Emotionally Disturbed Person.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>情绪困扰人员（Emotionally Disturbed Person）。

00:48:53.620 --> 00:48:56.700
<v Michael Marino>Son, you've caused this.
<v Michael Marino>年轻人，这是你自找的。

00:48:56.700 --> 00:48:58.050
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>I didn't cause anything.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>我什么都没做。

00:48:58.050 --> 00:49:11.330
<v Michael Marino>You have caused this. Now you have a choice. They're saying you have to go to the hospital. That's EMS. These are trained medical professionals. And if you don't go, then you're not acting rationally. And they say now they're afraid you're emotionally disturbed.
<v Michael Marino>这就是你自找的。现在你有一个选择。他们说你必须去医院。那是急救人员。这些是受过培训的医疗专业人员。如果你不去，那你就是在表现得不理智。他们说现在他们担心你情绪失常。

00:49:11.330 --> 00:49:24.550
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>It was all very surreal. At that point right there, he's very agitated. His face is red, and I knew then that anything could happen. I had no witnesses. No one was living with me.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>这一切都太超现实了。就在那个时候，他非常激动。他的脸通红，我当时就知道任何事情都可能发生。我没有证人。没有人跟我一起住。

00:49:24.550 --> 00:49:27.970
<v Michael Marino>So you have a choice. What is it going to be?
<v Michael Marino>所以你有一个选择。到底怎么样？

00:49:27.970 --> 00:49:30.250
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>I'm laying right here until I feel better.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>我就躺在这里直到我感觉好点。

00:49:30.250 --> 00:49:34.870
<v Michael Marino>OK, son. He's EDP. He's EDP.
<v Michael Marino>好吧，年轻人。他是EDP。他是EDP。

00:49:34.870 --> 00:49:35.860
<v Police Officer>Put your hands behind your back.
<v Police Officer>把你的双手背到身后。

00:49:35.860 --> 00:49:38.240
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>Why am I putting my hands behind my back?
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>我为什么要双手背到身后？

00:49:38.240 --> 00:49:41.740
<v Michael Marino>Because you have to go to the hosptial. All right, just take him. I can't [BLEEP] understand him anymore.
<v Michael Marino>因为你必须去医院。好了，直接带他走。我他妈的再也听不懂他在说什么了。

00:49:41.740 --> 00:49:42.990
<v Police Officer>Adrian, come here. Put your hands behind your back.
<v Police Officer>阿德里安，过来。把手背到身后。

00:49:42.990 --> 00:49:43.910
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>[GRUNTS]
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>[闷哼声]

00:49:43.910 --> 00:49:44.900
<v Police Officer>Get your hands behind your back.
<v Police Officer>把手背到身后去。

00:49:44.900 --> 00:49:45.820
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>[GRUNTS]
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>[闷哼声]

00:49:45.820 --> 00:49:47.960
<v Police Officer>Get one hand. Go ahead. Get one hand.
<v Police Officer>抓住一只手。上。抓住一只手。

00:49:47.960 --> 00:49:57.760
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>They pulled me off the bed. They slammed me to the floor. The way they were stomping on my back, they were pressing on my chest in a way that it was affecting my circulation.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>他们把我从床上拉下来。把我狠狠摔在地板上。他们踩在我背上的方式、他们压迫我胸部的方式，已经影响了我的血液循环。

00:49:57.760 --> 00:49:59.030
<v Michael Marino>Adrian stop it.
<v Michael Marino>阿德里安，住手。

00:49:59.030 --> 00:50:02.680
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>My chest. Oh, my chest.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>我的胸口。哦，我的胸口。

00:50:02.680 --> 00:50:10.010
<v Ira Glass>During the struggle, as they cuff Adrian, the little recorder falls out of his pocket. Deputy Chief Marino spots it.
<v Ira Glass>在扭打过程中，当他们给阿德里安戴上手铐时，那个小型录音机从他口袋里掉了出来。副局长马里诺一眼就看到了它。

00:50:10.010 --> 00:50:23.780
<v Michael Marino>Absolutely amazing, Adrian. You put your fellow police officers through this. Absolutely amazing. Yeah, it's a recorder. Recording devices, and everything else-- so he's playing a game here. Cute.
<v Michael Marino>真是太了不起了，阿德里安。你让你的同行警察经历这一切。真是太了不起了。对，是个录音机。录音设备以及其他一切——所以他在这里玩游戏呢。真可爱。

00:50:23.780 --> 00:50:27.140
<v Ira Glass>So if he found that recorder, how are we hearing this tape?
<v Ira Glass>既然他发现了那个录音机，我们是怎么听到这段磁带的？

00:50:27.140 --> 00:50:34.850
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>No, he found the recorder that was in my pocket. There was another recorder. The one that was running was just a recorder on the shelf.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>不，他找到的是我口袋里的那个录音机。还有另一个录音机。正在运行的那个只是放在书架上的录音机。

00:50:34.850 --> 00:50:36.170
<v Ira Glass>In plain sight?
<v Ira Glass>大庭广众之下？

00:50:36.170 --> 00:50:38.750
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>I had some books around it.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>我周围放了一些书把它挡住了。

00:50:38.750 --> 00:50:56.830
<v Ira Glass>Now that Deputy Chief Marino has labeled Schoolcraft EDP, the police take Schoolcraft and commit him to a psychiatric ward, saying he was a danger to himself. Schoolcraft, who had spent months documenting his bosses telling cops to lock people up on contrived pretenses, now found himself locked up on contrived pretenses.
<v Ira Glass>既然副局长马里诺已经将斯库尔克拉夫特标记为情绪困扰人员（EDP），警方便将斯库尔克拉夫特带走并关进了精神病房，称他对自身构成危险。斯库尔克拉夫特花了几个月时间记录他的上司指使警察以捏造的借口抓人，而现在他发现自己正因捏造的借口而被关押起来。

00:50:56.830 --> 00:51:10.090
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>They told the hospital staff that I left work early, I yelled at my supervisor-- and I swore at my supervisors, cursed at them-- that I ran from them, and I barricaded myself in my home.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>他们告诉医院工作人员说我提前下班，我对主管大喊大叫——我对主管爆粗口、咒骂他们——说我从他们那里逃跑，还将自己反锁在家中。

00:51:10.090 --> 00:51:12.170
<v Ira Glass>But the tapes showed that isn't true.
<v Ira Glass>但磁带显示事实并非如此。

00:51:12.170 --> 00:51:14.620
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>Correct, no. None of that happened.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>没错，不是的。那些都没有发生。

00:51:14.620 --> 00:51:31.690
<v Ira Glass>Schoolcraft's father, the last person Schoolcraft talked to, is unable to find him for days. The last he heard, his son was in an apartment surrounded by police, the next, he just vanished. His father says he called Internal Affairs, the FBI, the press. Finally he located him by calling around the hospitals all over Queens.
<v Ira Glass>斯库尔克拉夫特的父亲是斯库尔克拉夫特联系过的最后一个人，他连着几天都找不到儿子。他听到的最后消息是儿子在被警察包围的公寓里，转眼间儿子就凭空消失了。他的父亲说他打电话给内务部、联邦调查局、媒体。最后他是通过给皇后区各家医院打电话才找到了他。

00:51:31.690 --> 00:51:46.900
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>That's the only way I got out, because he confronted the hospital administration and said, here's my son's health care proxy, I'm his father. Why have you imprisoned my son here? And they had no answer, and they had to release me.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>我能出来全靠这个，因为他与医院管理层对质并说道：“这是我儿子的医疗代理权文件，我是他父亲。你们凭什么把我儿子关在这里？”他们答不上话，只好把我释放了。

00:51:46.900 --> 00:51:49.440
<v Ira Glass>Why do you think they went so far with you?
<v Ira Glass>你认为他们为什么对你采取这么极端的手段？

00:51:49.440 --> 00:51:54.810
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>It seemed like an act of desperation. Panic.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>这看起来像是绝望的行为。恐慌。

00:51:54.810 --> 00:51:56.920
<v Graham Rayman>You can look at it in a couple of different ways.
<v Graham Rayman>你可以从几个不同的角度来看待这件事。

00:51:56.920 --> 00:51:58.540
<v Ira Glass>Again, reporter Graham Rayman.
<v Ira Glass>再次请出记者格雷姆·雷曼。

00:51:58.540 --> 00:52:08.720
<v Graham Rayman>One is that they put him in the psych ward because he tried to report corruption and misconduct. They literally tried to destroy his reputation.
<v Graham Rayman>一种可能是，他们把他关进精神病房，是因为他试图举报腐败和渎职行为。他们从字面意义上试图摧毁他的名誉。

00:52:08.720 --> 00:52:11.140
<v Ira Glass>Like, he's literally crazy. That's the message.
<v Ira Glass>就好像，他真的疯了。这就是他们要传达的信息。

00:52:11.140 --> 00:52:28.400
<v Graham Rayman>Yeah, right. That they were trying to portray him as crazy. You could also look at it-- that the chief lost his temper that night. Just got angry and gave an order that turns out to be a totally inappropriate order. I could see that being the case also.
<v Graham Rayman>对，没错。他们试图把他描绘成一个疯子。你也可以这样看——那位长官那天失去了理智。只是发火并下达了一个后来证明完全不合适的命令。我也能理解可能是这种情况。

00:52:28.400 --> 00:53:15.310
<v Ira Glass>At the time that he led the raid on Schoolcraft's apartment, Deputy Chief Michael Marino was already under a microscope. It was just a month after he had been put on trial inside the department after a sting named him as one of 27 cops who illegally bought human growth hormone, or steroids. Marino claimed that he used the human growth hormone for a medical condition. And back in 2006, an arbitrator found that Marino was in violation of New York labor laws for a very similar situation to the one that Schoolcraft was documenting. The arbitrator ruled that Marino had set up an illegal quota for police officers of four parking tickets, three moving violations, three quality of life summons, and two stop-and-frisk per month and then penalized the officers when they didn't make the quota.
<v Ira Glass>在带队搜查斯库尔克拉夫特的公寓时，副局长迈克尔·马里诺已经处在风口浪尖上。就在一个月前，他刚刚在警局内部接受听证，此前一项卧底行动指出他是非法购买人类生长激素或类固醇的27名警察之一。马里诺声称他使用人类生长激素是为了治疗某种疾病。而在2006年，一名仲裁员曾裁定马里诺违反了纽约劳动法，其情况与斯库尔克拉夫特所记录的经历极其相似。仲裁员裁定，马里诺曾为警员设定了非法的每月指标——四张停车罚单、三张交通违章罚单、三张生活质量传票以及两次拦下盘查，并在警员未达成指标时对其进行惩罚。

00:53:15.310 --> 00:53:17.510
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>I didn't figure I would lose my job.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>我当时没想过我会丢掉工作。

00:53:17.510 --> 00:53:22.090
<v Ira Glass>Adrian Schoolcraft says that in the end, none of this worked out the way he thought it would during all those months of recording.
<v Ira Glass>阿德里安·斯库尔克拉夫特说，到头来，这一切的发展跟他这几个月录音时的设想完全不一样。

00:53:22.090 --> 00:53:37.030
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>I figured someone would approach the supervisor and say, listen you got caught. Knock it off. And everything's in house, still. Just knock it off. This is getting out of control. I never saw myself as an adversary.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>我以为会有人找到主管，然后说，听着，你们被抓包了。别这么干了。事情依然是在内部解决。只要收手就行。这已经失控了。我从没把自己当成对立面。

00:53:37.030 --> 00:53:42.760
<v Ira Glass>Because you assumed that the police commissioner-- the people at the very top of the police force-- that they would be on your side.
<v Ira Glass>因为你以为警察局长——警队最高层的人——会站在你这边。

00:53:42.760 --> 00:53:43.950
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>Correct.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>没错。

00:53:43.950 --> 00:53:47.800
<v Ira Glass>But now do you believe that, in fact, they would be on your side?
<v Ira Glass>但现在你相信他们事实上会站在你这边吗？

00:53:47.800 --> 00:53:51.250
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>I don't believe they were, or ever intended to be.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>我不认为他们曾经站在我这边，也没打算过。

00:53:51.250 --> 00:54:15.050
<v Ira Glass>That's the question, of course. And there's really no way to know how typical the 81st precinct is. Reporter Graham Rayman has heard from retired cops who say the same things happened where they worked. And he's found a policeman who was secretly recording in the Bronx at the same time as Schoolcraft finding the same things. The guys who study the way CompStat is used by the police, John Eterno and Eli Silverman, say manipulating stats to get better numbers seems to happen in a lot of places where CompStat is used.
<v Ira Glass>当然，这才是问题所在。而且根本没有办法知道第81分局究竟有多典型。记者格雷厄姆·雷曼听到过退休警察讲述类似的事情在他们工作过的地方发生。他还找到了一名警察，这名警察在布朗克斯秘密录音的时间和斯库尔克拉夫特同期，也发现了同样的情况。研究警方如何使用警情统计系统的专家约翰·埃特诺和伊利·西尔弗曼表示，为了获得更好看的数据而操纵统计数字的现象，似乎在使用警情统计系统的许多地方都会发生。

00:54:15.050 --> 00:54:28.770
<v Eli Silverman>There's evidence of the same kind of distortion-- we've done research, where people have written in our blog-- from other countries, UK, Australia, as well. Commanders attesting to the same phenomenon. This is not unique to New York.
<v Eli Silverman>有证据表明存在同类的歪曲现象——我们做过研究，人们在我们的博客上留言——来自英国、澳大利亚等其他国家也是如此。指挥官们也证实了这种现象。这并非纽约独有。

00:54:28.770 --> 00:55:13.770
<v Ira Glass>Having failed to reach any results working inside the department, Schoolcraft finally went to the press. And Graham's five-part series in The Village Voice has been, Adrian says, like a meteor hitting the 81st precinct. The police commissioner transferred Commander Stephen Mauriello, and some of the other senior-level supervisors, out of the precinct. Though he only did that after several weeks of pressure from politicians and clergy. There's now one police investigation into Schoolcraft's allegations, there's another investigation of Deputy Chief Marino's order to put Schoolcraft into a psych ward, another into the charge that serious crimes were downgraded to lesser ones, and a fourth that is just about the misclassification of crimes in Detective Hernandez's sexual assault case. Schoolcraft's recordings will be used in two class action lawsuits, one about stop-and-frisks, one about quotas. Schoolcraft himself is suing the department for $50 million. Two officers have come forward to back up his charges. A website, schoolcraftjustice.com has been set up looking for more. Schoolcraft himself is suspended without pay, living with his dad, 350 miles away, in upstate New York-- where, he says, a dozen times city police have shown up and pounded on his door, yelling, "NYPD, we know you're in there. Open up." [KNOCKING] Of course, he recorded it.
<v Ira Glass>在警局内部没有取得任何结果后，斯库尔克拉夫特最终找到了媒体。格雷厄姆在《乡村之声》上发表的五部分系列报道，阿德里安说，就像一颗流星砸中了第81分局。警察局长将指挥官斯蒂芬·毛里埃洛以及其他一些高级别主管调离了该分局。尽管他是在政界人士和神职人员施加了数周压力之后才这么做的。目前有一项针对斯库尔克拉夫特指控的警察内部调查，还有另一项调查针对副局长马里诺将斯库尔克拉夫特送进精神病房的命令，第三项调查针对严重犯罪被降级为较轻罪行的指控，第四项则专门针对埃尔南德斯侦探的性侵案中犯罪分类错误的问题。斯库尔克拉夫特的录音将被用于两起集体诉讼，一起关于拦下盘查，另一起关于指标。斯库尔克拉夫特本人正起诉警局并索赔5000万美元。两名警官站出来支持他的指控。一个名为 schoolcraftjustice.com 的网站已经建立，旨在寻找更多证据。斯库尔克拉夫特本人目前处于停薪留职状态，和父亲住在纽约北部350英里外的地方——他说，在那里，市警察已经十几次出现在他门前，疯狂砸门并大喊：“纽约警察局，我们知道你在里面。开门。”[敲门声]当然，他把这个录音了。

00:55:42.510 --> 00:55:56.850
<v Police Officer>Adrian, we know you're in there. Just open the door please, so we can get back to New York.
<v Police Officer>阿德里安，我们知道你在里面。请把门打开，好让我们回纽约。

00:55:56.850 --> 00:56:01.550
<v Ira Glass>Schoolcraft assumes that he'll never again work as a police officer anywhere.
<v Ira Glass>斯库尔克拉夫特认为他再也不可能在任何地方当警察了。

00:56:01.550 --> 00:56:03.780
<v Ira Glass>Is it weird not to be a policeman anymore?
<v Ira Glass>不再当警察感觉怪怪的吗？

00:56:03.780 --> 00:56:17.520
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>It feels odd. But I still feel like I am a policeman. I'm going forward with this investigation. I just feel like this is my case. This is the one. And I'll go all the way with it.
<v Adrian Schoolcraft>感觉怪怪的。但我仍然觉得我是一名警察。我正在继续推进这项调查。我只是觉得这是我的案子。这就是那个案子。我会奉陪到底的。

00:56:17.520 --> 00:57:02.520
<v Ira Glass>And finally, with the 81st precinct under new supervision, the numbers on serious crime have risen by 10-15%. Are the crimes going up, or that's closer to the true amount of crime that was already there, only now being recorded? [MUSIC - "OFFICER" BY THE PHARCYDE] Well, our program today was produced by me and Sarah Koenig, with Alex Blumberg, Ben Calhoun, Jane Feeltes, Jonathan Menjivar, Lisa Pollak, Robin Semien, and Alissa Shipp and Nancy Updike. Our senior producer is Julie Snyder. Seth Lind is our production manager. Emily Condon's our office manager. Music help from Jessica Hopper. Production help from Shawn Wen. [ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS] This American Life is distributed by Public Radio International. WBEZ management oversight of our program by our boss, Mr. Torey Malatia, who's got no problem with the end of Don't Ask, Don't Tell. Seriously.
<v Ira Glass>最后，随着第81分局迎来新的管理层，严重犯罪的数据上升了10%到15%。是犯罪率上升了，还是这更接近原本就已经存在、只是现在才被记录下来的真实犯罪数量？[音乐 - 费尔西德乐队的《军官》] 好吧，我们今天的节目由我和莎拉·科尼格制作，参与者还有亚历克斯·布隆伯格、本·卡尔霍恩、简·菲尔特斯、乔纳森·门吉瓦尔、丽莎·波拉克、罗宾·塞米恩、阿莉莎·希普以及南希·厄普代克。我们的高级制作人是朱莉·斯奈德。赛斯·林德是我们的制作经理。埃米莉·康登是我们的办公室经理。音乐协助来自杰西卡·霍珀。制作协助来自肖恩·温。[鸣谢] 本期《美国生活》节目由国际公共广播电台发行。WBEZ对我方节目的管理监督由我们的老板托雷·马拉蒂亚先生负责，他对“不问，不说”政策的结束没有任何意见。说真的。

00:57:28.460 --> 00:57:33.040
<v Joe Lipari>No, I have a gay cousin. I am the least homophobic person in the world.
<v Joe Lipari>不，我有一个同性恋表亲。我是世界上最不恐同的人。

00:57:33.040 --> 00:57:38.040
<v Ira Glass>I'm Ira Glass. Back next week with more stories of This American Life.
<v Ira Glass>我是艾拉·格拉斯。下周将带回更多《美国生活》的故事。
